# Main permission retry: AF_UNIX datagram socket

In diagnostic002, `process-stderr.log` and structured review show repeated real `PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted` at the S1 progress mailbox's `socket.socket(AF_UNIX, SOCK_DGRAM)` call. Main inspected exact terminal, receipt, execution and retirement first: outer session64795 and child PID3 both completed with exit1; child was matched-waited and absent afterward. No replay of the diagnostic or any successful write occurred.

Repository sandbox policy required one outside-sandbox retry of that exact restricted socket-creation operation. The one retry command was `python3 -c 'import socket; s=socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX,socket.SOCK_DGRAM); s.close(); print("AF_UNIX datagram socket creation and close passed")'` with `sandbox_permissions=require_escalated`, prefix `["python3"]`. It succeeded and immediately closed the local socket. It contacted no service and ran no project test. This establishes the sandbox restriction for socket creation. Any next Plan049 run must have a reviewed explicit permission mode matching its actual tool invocation; do not merely reissue the old `use_default` command or use a substitute transport.

This record does not authorize a second unrestricted retry or a full suite launch by itself. Main requests a narrow Plan049 correction and independent review to represent the exact bounded runtime `require_escalated` mode in the session-proof start-argument contract, preserving every other binding, ownership/cap, no-timeout and acceptance rule. No explicit denial or missing allow rule occurred.
